  "note": "Annual election of the Newtownards Urban Council, January 1927. Five vacancies, one in each of the town's five wards. The Belfast News-Letter reports that, except for Mr. W. Lamont Doggart, the old members were renominated and that Mr. James Freeland was nominated for the fifth vacancy; there were no other nominations and the five were returned unopposed. The paper does not attach the names to individual wards, so they are recorded together for the borough. Retiring members were Messrs. W. H. Simms (chairman), S. H. Black, W. Lamont Doggart, T. Allan Brett, and John Malcolmson, 'representing the five wards of the town'. Doggart did not seek re-election; James Freeland, an ex-member, was nominated for his vacancy. Returned unopposed."
